# Module

::READ (Construct: Tag) FROM `../expressions/tag.art`.
::READ (Construct: NaturalName) FROM `../expressions/natural-name.art`.
::READ (Construct: NaturalBlock) FROM `./natural-block.art`.

## Construct: SectionBlock

**Category:** Structural

**Purpose:** Capture named sections — the key construct that turns a markdown heading into a named resource that modules can reference, index, and project.

**Description:** A SectionBlock is a structural construct consisting of a heading and its associated content. The heading text is the section name, taken verbatim after tag extraction — `# Checkout: Art Work` names one section `Checkout: Art Work`; the construct never splits the text. It is the bridge between the grammar and modules layers: the grammar fixes the form (name, tags, content), while the meaning of each resource is provided by the structures — the domain declarations in `.art`. Higher layers that interpret headings as `Kind: Name` resources do that parsing themselves, downstream. Closed syntax, open semantics.

<!-- refine content rules -->

**Schema:**

```
SectionBlock {
    name: string           // section name: the whole heading text, tags stripped
    tags?: Tag[]           // optional projection tags
    content: NaturalBlock  // associated content (catch-all classification)
}
```

**Syntax:**

```art
<SectionBlock> =
    # <name> [<Tags>]
    <NaturalBlock>
```

**Rules:**

- A SectionBlock MUST define a name.
- A SectionBlock declares a resource identified by its name.
- A SectionBlock MAY be tagged with one or more Tag.
- A SectionBlock MAY contain arbitrary content.
- A SectionBlock MAY contain nested SectionBlocks.

**Examples:**

Example of Section Block.

```md
## Rules

Lorem ipsum
```

Example of Section Block whose heading text contains a colon — the text stays one name.

```md
### Rule: Maximum 4 items

This is a rule.
```

Example of Section Block with tags.

```md
### Routine: List Tasks (#generator) (#wip)

**Purpose:** List tasks according to criteria, ...
```
